259:     /**
260:      * Gets the parallelism with which operation are executed by default. Operations can
261:      * individually override this value to use a specific parallelism.
262:      *
263:      * <p>Other operations may need to run with a different parallelism - for example calling a
264:      * reduce operation over the entire data set will involve an operation that runs with a
265:      * parallelism of one (the final reduce to the single result value).
266:      *
267:      * @return The parallelism used by operations, unless they override that value. This method
268:      *     returns {@link #PARALLELISM_DEFAULT} if the environment's default parallelism should be
269:      *     used.
270:      */
271:     public int getParallelism() {
272:         return configuration.get(CoreOptions.DEFAULT_PARALLELISM);
273:     }
